[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oggii/enshrouded-shared-xp/main/nexus/banner.jpg[/img][/center]

[b]New in 1.1.2:[/b] a chat line when a player joins: [i]"Shared XP 1.1.2 is active: non-combat XP is shared with everyone online."[/i] No line = the mod is off (for example after your host installed a game update). Turn it off with [b]AnnounceInChat=0[/b].
[b]1.1.1:[/b] works on the 20 October server update (build 26083076) as well as build 25988414.
[b]1.1.0:[/b] optional combat XP sharing ([b]ShareCombatXp=1[/b]) for players far from the kill.

[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
When one player earns XP from exploring, reading books and notes, quests, mining or completing item sets, every other player who is online gets the same amount. Distance does not matter: you can mine in one corner of the map while your friend explores the other, and you both level up.

Combat XP is left to the game by default (it already shares it with players near the kill). Turn on [b]ShareCombatXp[/b] and players far from a kill get the same XP as the players at the kill, so a friend who is mining keeps up with a friend who is fighting.

[b]Server-side only.[/b] Players install nothing and join as usual. A few seconds after joining, the chat confirms that the mod is running.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[b]Windows server[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Stop the server.
[*]Copy [i]powrprof.dll[/i] and [i]xpshare.ini[/i] into the folder with [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i].
[*]Start the server.
[/list]
[b]Linux / Docker (Wine)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Stop the container.
[*]Copy [i]powrprof.dll[/i] and [i]xpshare.ini[/i] next to [i]enshrouded_server.exe[/i].
[*]Add the environment variable [i]WINEDLLOVERRIDES=powrprof=n,b[/i].
[*]Start the container.
[/list]
[b]Check:[/b] join the server; after a few seconds the chat shows [i]"Shared XP 1.1.2 is active ..."[/i]. No line? Look at [i]xpshare.log[/i] next to the server exe: it says why (after a game update usually [i]unknown server build[/i]). On a working server the log shows "active on server build ...: non-combat XP is shared with every online player".

[b]Uninstall:[/b] stop the server and delete powrprof.dll, xpshare.ini and xpshare.log.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Shares exploration, lore, quest, mining and item-set XP with every online player, at any distance.
[*][b]Multiplier[/b] (default 1.0): shared XP = the other player's gain x this value. 0.5 = half.
[*][b]DoubleQuestXp[/b] (default 0): quests finished together give everyone the quest XP once. Set 1 to also add the others' share (double quest XP).
[*][b]ShareCombatXp[/b] (default 0): set 1 to share combat XP too. Players far from a kill get the XP the players at the kill got, once per kill; players at the kill get nothing extra.
[*][b]AnnounceInChat[/b] (default 1): one chat line when a player joins, so everybody sees in game that the mod is active. Needs text chat enabled on the server. Set 0 to turn it off.
[*][b]Safe on game updates:[/b] on an unknown server build the mod does nothing and the server runs as usual. You notice it in game: the chat line does not come.
[*][b]LogEveryShare[/b]: 1 logs every gain and share, handy to check it works.
[*]Opens no ports and sends nothing anywhere.
[/list]
Settings live in [i]xpshare.ini[/i]; restart the server after changes.

[b]Good to know[/b]
[list]
[*]Only players who are online receive shared XP. There is no catch-up for offline players.
[*]Shared XP shows no "+XP" popup in game, but the XP bar and level go up.
[*]With DoubleQuestXp=0, shared quest XP arrives about 5 seconds after the quest.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Enshrouded 1.0 dedicated server, Steam builds [b]25988414[/b] and [b]26083076[/b] (October 2026). After a game update, wait for an updated version.
[*]Windows server, or Linux/Docker under Wine (tested with mornedhels/enshrouded-server:1.7.2-wine).
[*]Access to the server folder, and to environment variables on Linux hosts.
[*]No other mods needed.
[/list]
Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/oggii/enshrouded-shared-xp]github.com/oggii/enshrouded-shared-xp[/url]. Some antivirus tools flag proxy DLLs by heuristics; you can read the code and build the DLL yourself.

[size=4][b]Shout outs[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The earlier XP share mod (Nexus #110) for the idea of distance-free XP sharing. This is a new implementation for Enshrouded 1.0.
[*][url=https://github.com/cursey/safetyhook]SafetyHook[/url] and [url=https://github.com/zyantific/zydis]Zydis[/url] for the hooking.
[*]Keen Games for Enshrouded.
[/list]
